<!-- Section 7: Twelve practical examples -->
<section id="sec-practical" class="mx-auto mt-12 w-full max-w-4xl section-shell prose-shell scroll-mt-24">
  <h2>Real-World Applications of Right Triangle Area From Two Legs</h2>
  <p>Twelve worked situations carry the formula from the page into the workshop, the site, and the studio. Each one names a right-triangular panel, section, profile, or simplified model, works the two calculator inputs through the formula, and states the assumption behind the numbers. Where the real object is curved or irregular, the calculation covers the modeled triangle only, and the area never stands in for strength, cost, or safety on its own.</p>

  <h3>Example 1: Triangular Glass Window</h3>
  <p>A triangular glass window has perpendicular dimensions of <span set:html={rich('[[a=3\\text{ m}]]')} />, <span set:html={rich('[[b=4\\text{ m}]]')} />. Substitute: <span set:html={rich('[[K=\\frac{3\\times4}{2}]]')} />, <span set:html={rich('[[[\\boxed{K=6\\text{ m}^2}]]]')} />. The result represents the flat glass surface before frame dimensions are subtracted. Assumption: the pane is a true right triangle; the frame allowance is handled separately.</p>

  <h3>Example 2: Steel Support Bracket</h3>
  <p>A triangular steel bracket has <span set:html={rich('[[a=5\\text{ cm}]]')} />, <span set:html={rich('[[b=12\\text{ cm}]]')} />. Then <span set:html={rich('[[K=\\frac{5\\times12}{2}]]')} />, <span set:html={rich('[[[\\boxed{K=30\\text{ cm}^2}]]]')} />. The area describes the flat plate and does not determine its load-bearing capacity. Assumption: the bracket blank is cut as a right triangle; bolt holes and bends are excluded.</p>

  <h3>Example 3: Triangular Ramp Side Profile</h3>
  <p>A simplified ramp side profile has <span set:html={rich('[[a=6\\text{ m}]]')} />, <span set:html={rich('[[b=8\\text{ m}]]')} />. Then <span set:html={rich('[[K=\\frac{6\\times8}{2}]]')} />, <span set:html={rich('[[[\\boxed{K=24\\text{ m}^2}]]]')} />. This is the vertical triangular side profile, not the sloping walking surface. Assumption: the profile is modeled with a square corner at the base.</p>

  <h3>Example 4: Triangular Roof Support</h3>
  <p>A triangular roof support section has <span set:html={rich('[[a=8\\text{ ft}]]')} />, <span set:html={rich('[[b=15\\text{ ft}]]')} />. Then <span set:html={rich('[[K=\\frac{8\\times15}{2}]]')} />, <span set:html={rich('[[[\\boxed{K=60\\text{ ft}^2}]]]')} />. The area represents the flat triangular section, useful for material estimates. Assumption: the section is modeled as a right triangle; the full roof geometry may differ.</p>

  <h3>Example 5: Right-Triangular Garden Section</h3>
