  <h2>Two Measurements, One Halved Product</h2>
  <p>Two perpendicular lengths are enough. Multiply them, halve the product, and the enclosed surface is named. The rectangle proof shows why the halving is exact rather than conventional, the Pythagorean theorem checks the sides behind the answer, and the rearranged formula recovers a missing leg when the area is already known.</p>
  <p>The working habit is simple: confirm the 90-degree corner, match the units, keep decimals unrounded until the end, and verify through the rectangle. With those habits, <span set:html={rich('[[K=\\frac{ab}{2}]]')} /> is the most dependable area calculation in geometry.</p>
</section>
